# AI and Emerging Technologies

## AI-Powered Personalized Learning

**Emerging technology:** AI-powered personalized learning
**Focus:** How artificial intelligence can adapt learning activities and feedback to individual students

### a. What emerging technology did you choose? How is AI being used to support it?

AI-native Dev platforms is the emerging tech that I chose for this assignment.  These platforms, like Claude Code, help software engineers write code, explain the code, and help them fix code.  This allows teams, or engineers, to build faster and more securely. I used this at my last job at a bank where incorporating this technology was meant to help us do more with less. I used it to write unit tests rather than writing them myself.

### b. What solutions were used before AI? How has AI replaced or will soon replace them?

All my coding work was done manually within IDEs and auto-fill but all the tests and security checks were manual.  Claude Code helped automate those security checks so I could clean up the code and properly test the code prior to pushing to Production.

### c. What type of AI is used?
For the most part, this was generative and not agentic.  I was able to type what I needed as I could understand it, and it would help me write the code behind it.

### d. How does the use of AI and this technology affect everyday life?

For me, I was able to spend less time writing the manual tests and foundational code and focus more on the logic itself to meet business requirements.  AI gave me the general basis and I could go from there more easily.

### e. Are there any concerns with using AI for this application?

In general, yes, AI can make mistakes and is meant to perform a task and can skip security or come up with passable tests that don't really test true functionality if it is really just trying to get the code to work. Having a 'human in the loop' is still required to make sure AI does not hallucinate with too much context and security stays top of mind.

